# maprange — a walk over a Go map is made canonical before anything it feeds is
# rendered; an answer is a function of the instance, never of map iteration
# order (INVARIANTS.md H-16).
#
# The surface is derived by internal/surfaceaudit.MapRangeSurface: every
# `range` statement in the module's non-test sources whose expression is a map,
# found with go/types across every build-tag configuration the sources declare.
# A parser cannot see half of these (a struct field, a named map type), and a
# hand sweep saw all of them exactly once — 2026-07-26, when it found
# `companion wireguard status` printing one arbitrary entry of m.Resolved — and
# was never run again. This ledger is that sweep, standing.
#
# No AST can prove sortedness, so each line carries the judgment a reviewer
# made about the walk: `proven` names a test that pins the fed output
# byte-identical across runs; `exempt` states why the order is structurally
# unobservable (a set is built, a slice is sorted before use, a single-key map
# is length-guarded, a store re-orders on read). A new walk is unclassified
# and fails the gate the day it appears.
#
# The ceiling is the number of walks known to be unproven. It may fall without
# ceremony and may only rise by editing this line on purpose.
#ceiling 0

# --- walks that feed rendered output, pinned deterministic by a test ----------
internal/analyze/trace.go:sortedStepPaths = proven: TestSortedStepPaths_NumericSegments
internal/cmd/ent.go:findAreaNeighbors = proven: TestDedupeAndSortRelated_Canonical
internal/cmd/ent.go:findDeviceSiblings = proven: TestDedupeAndSortRelated_Canonical
internal/cmd/flow.go:sortedKeys = proven: TestRenderFlowResult_ErrorsAreDeterministic
internal/haapi/flow.go:parseMenuOptions = proven: TestRenderFlowResult_MenuStep
internal/haapi/servicedata.go:(*ServiceDescriptor).AcceptedFields = proven: TestAcceptedFieldsFlattensSectionsAndIsSorted
internal/haapi/servicedata.go:(*ServiceDescriptor).UnknownFields = proven: TestUnknownFieldsRefusesWhatHomeAssistantRefuses
internal/cmd/wireguard_cmd.go:writeWireguardMonitor = proven: TestWriteWireguardStatus_ResolvedRenderIsDeterministic

# --- walks whose order is destroyed before anything reads it ------------------
internal/cmd/ent.go:runEntShow = exempt: collects the unshown attribute keys into a slice that is sort.Strings-ed before the render loop reads it
internal/cmd/ent_who.go:runEntWho = exempt: tallies trigger counts into summary rows sorted by a total order (count desc, then trigger asc) before rendering
internal/cmd/rtfm.go:runRTFMFamilies = exempt: groups aliases per family and sort.Strings-es each family's slice before rendering; family order comes from the fixed Families() slice
internal/degeneracy/degeneracy.go:(*collector).err = exempt: collects the missing-field keys and sort.Strings them before composing the error text
internal/manual/families.go:FamilyMembers = exempt: collects the aliases pointing at one family and sort.Strings-es the slice before returning it, so the name every banner and refusal interpolates is fixed (TestFamilyMembersCoversTheAliasesPointingAtIt asserts sortedness directly)
internal/hatest/recorder.go:knownSchemaVersions = exempt: collects the schema versions and sort.Ints them before joining into the message
internal/cmd/policy_typed.go:scriptCreatePlan = exempt: a single-key map, length-guarded (len(top) == 1) before the walk, which reads its one key
internal/surfaceaudit/boolcell.go:handRolledBoolWords = exempt: collects the identifiers assigned more than one bool word and sort.Strings-es the slice before returning it, so the site keys a manifest is written against never move
internal/jsonwalk/jsonwalk.go:sortedKeys = exempt: this IS a canonicalizer — it collects keys and sort.Strings them so every YAML/JSON walk visits children in one order
internal/surfaceaudit/surface.go:Check = exempt: the stale-entry sweep appends to a slice that is sort.Strings-ed before the report renders
internal/testaudit/assertions.go:scanDir = exempt: ScanRepo sorts the combined tests by file and line before any caller reads them

# --- walks whose order is structurally unobservable ---------------------------
internal/cmd/cache.go:refreshTracesFromHA = exempt: rows land in SQLite and every read back out orders by start_time in the query, so the walk's order never reaches an answer
internal/cmd/helper.go:helperCreateID = exempt: guarded by len(top) != 1 just above, so the walk visits exactly one key — there is no order to observe
internal/cmd/label.go:matchingLabelIDs = exempt: builds a set of label ids consumed by membership checks only; iteration order cannot reach output
internal/cmd/script.go:normalizeScriptCreateYAML = exempt: guarded by len(top) != 1 just above, so the walk visits exactly one key — there is no order to observe
internal/cmd/script.go:normalizeScriptYAML = exempt: entered only when len(top) == 1, so the walk visits exactly one key — there is no order to observe
internal/manual/state.go:loadSession = exempt: TTL eviction deletes expired sessions during the walk; nothing renders and the surviving set is order-independent
internal/mcpserver/gate.go:ClassifiedPaths = exempt: feeds the classification exhaustiveness tests, which compare membership in both directions; per-set slice order is never rendered
internal/surfaceaudit/scan.go:callArgsMention = exempt: membership scan returning a bool; no order is observable in the answer
internal/surfaceaudit/partialscope.go:calledNames = exempt: the names collected from the set are sorted before they are returned, so the site note is a function of the code rather than of map order
internal/hatest/recorder.go:verifyRecorderSchema = exempt: presence check over required columns; which missing column aborts first may vary, but that is the test rig refusing to run, never a command's answer
internal/testaudit/assertions.go:(*pkgScope).lookup = exempt: searches for a package-level func by name; Go allows one declaration per package, so every order finds the same answer
internal/testaudit/assertions.go:mergeNames = exempt: set union consumed by membership checks only; no order is observable
pkg/ids/ids.go:(*Registry).Load = exempt: rebuilds the reverse index; Mint refuses colliding short ids, so the pairs are unique and insertion order is immaterial

internal/haapi/flow.go:parseSelector = exempt: the walk is guarded to a map of exactly one entry — HA's `selector` object is `{"<kind>": {…}}` and anything else is refused before it — so there is no order for a canonicalisation to fix
internal/cmd/witness.go:loadWitness = exempt: the walk copies unexpired previews into a new map and feeds a key lookup, never an ordering; no output is derived from it
internal/realdata/helpers.go:HelperDomains = exempt: the walk builds a slice that is sort.Strings'd before it is returned, so the order of the walk is unobservable to every caller
internal/realdata/helpers.go:StorageCollections = exempt: the walk builds a map keyed by domain, one output file per key, and each file's item list is sorted by id before encoding — no output of this function is a function of the walk's order
internal/realdata/leak.go:Contains = proven: TestLeakReportIsOrderedByLocationNotByMapWalk
internal/realdata/configtext.go:ShapeDrift = proven: TestShapeDriftIsOrderedNotMapWalked
internal/realdata/bootability.go:ExclusionReport = proven: TestExclusionReportIsOrderedNotMapWalked

# --- the policy request classifier (internal/policy/reqmap) -------------------
internal/policy/reqmap/types.go:(*checkSet).list = proven: TestServiceChecksAreSortedAndUnique
internal/policy/reqmap/dashboard.go:DiffDashboard = proven: TestDiffDashboard
internal/policy/reqmap/service.go:serviceReach = proven: TestServiceCallMapping
internal/policy/reqmap/service.go:walkData = exempt: the walk only collects the mapping's keys, which are sort.Strings'd before any is visited
internal/policy/reqmap/wsmap.go:changedKeys = exempt: the walk builds a slice that is sort.Strings'd before it is returned
internal/policy/reqmap/rows.go:Rows = exempt: the walk builds a slice that is sorted by key before Rows returns it
internal/policy/reqmap/classify.go:classifyHTTP = exempt: merges extra query values key by key; no value's position depends on the order the keys are visited in
internal/policy/reqmap/companionmap.go:singleKey = exempt: walks a mapping already checked to hold exactly one key, so there is no order to observe
internal/policy/reqmap/dashboard.go:withoutViews = exempt: copies one map into another; the result is a map, compared with reflect.DeepEqual, never ranged
internal/surfaceaudit/policy.go:builderHelpers = exempt: a monotone fixpoint over caller sets that answers a set (map membership only); every visiting order reaches the same least fixpoint, and nothing it returns is ranged into output
internal/surfaceaudit/policy.go:onlyCalledBy = exempt: an all-of membership test returning a bool; no order is observable in the answer
internal/surfaceaudit/policycmd.go:PolicyCommandSites = exempt: collects the declared sinks that no longer exist and sort.Strings-es them before the error renders
internal/surfaceaudit/policycmd.go:(*callGraph).sinksReached = exempt: the sinks reached are collected and sort.Strings-ed before the site note renders, so the note is a function of the code, not of the walk
internal/surfaceaudit/policycmd.go:(*callGraph).indexStoredFuncs = exempt: fills a global-to-functions index only ever ranged as a set into the reachability walk, and gives each stored function literal a key that depends on the function alone; no visiting order is observable in what the census reports, which is sorted
internal/surfaceaudit/policycmd.go:loadCallGraph = exempt: builds indexes (by key, by file:line, the module's concrete types) that are only looked up or tested for membership; the one answer that depends on what they hold, a command's reached sinks, is sorted before it renders
internal/policy/enforce/session.go:(*Session).gather = exempt: copies the reach question's selectors from one map into another; the walk renders nothing and the order of a map's insertion has no meaning
internal/surfaceaudit/policy.go:productFiles = exempt: collects the union of every release target's product files into a set whose keys are sort.Strings-ed before anything parses or reports them
